This dedication covers everything Lexifina made: the history as commits, the commit messages and per-version notes,
the folder layout and file names, the indexes and tables (data/), the tools (tools/), the READMEs, REPRODUCE.md and
this file, from the first commit of this repository. It does not cover the texts listed in sections 2 and 3, which
come from their publishers and keep whatever terms those publishers give them. Nothing Lexifina made is under the MIT
License or any licence other than CC0 1.0.

2. The law: Copyright Act, 1957

2.1 Section 52(1)(q). The following do not constitute an infringement of copyright:
  "(q) the reproduction or publication of—
   (i) any matter which has been published in any Official Gazette except an Act of a Legislature;
   (ii) any Act of a Legislature subject to the condition that such Act is reproduced or published together with any
        commentary thereon or any other original matter;
   (iii) the report of any committee, commission, council, board or other like body appointed by the Government if
        such report has been laid on the Table of the Legislature, unless the reproduction or publication of such
        report is prohibited by the Government;
   (iv) any judgment or order of a court, tribunal or other judicial authority, unless the reproduction or
        publication of such judgment or order is prohibited by the court, the tribunal or other judicial authority,
        as the case may be;"
    (i) and (ii) as quoted below since 2026-11-03; (iii) and (iv) read from a secondary copy on 2026-11-21, to be
    checked against the official text when India Code can be read from here.
    Gazette matter other than Acts (rules, regulations, notifications, orders, ordinances) is taken under (i). Acts are
    published with original matter, as (ii) requires: the commit records of when each provision came into force and
    which law made it, the per-version notes, the tables in data/ and the tools in tools/. Judgments and orders are
    taken under (iv), official text only: no publisher's headnotes, summaries or paragraph numbering (Eastern Book
    Company v. D.B. Modak, Supreme Court, 2007).

2.2 Section 28 (Government works). Copyright in a Government work subsists for sixty years from the beginning of the
    calendar year next following the year in which the work is first published. Government works first published
    before 1966 (colonial and pre-1966 Acts, codes, regulations and gazettes) are therefore in the public domain in
    India, whatever a later copy or scan of them says.

2.3 Personal data and protected cases. Judgments in sexual-offence, POCSO, juvenile-justice and matrimonial cases are
    not included at all (Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita s.72, formerly IPC s.228A; POCSO Act s.23; Juvenile Justice Act 2015
    s.74; the Supreme Court's directions on anonymity). Paths and commit trailers name cases by number and CNR, never
    by party.

3. Texts from their publishers

3.0 Sources and their own terms (read on the dates given)

  e-Gazette, egazette.gov.in, formerly egazette.nic.in (Directorate of Printing / Department of Publication, Ministry
    of Housing and Urban Affairs): the Gazette of India, Extraordinary and Weekly. Its About page (read 2026-11-02)
    says the Gazette of India "can be accessed free of cost by the general public being available in the public
    domain"; its Disclaimer page has no body text; no prohibition on reproduction was found. robots.txt: none (404,
    read 2026-11-21).
  Legislative Department file store, cdnbbsr.s3waas.gov.in (the file store of legislative.gov.in, Ministry of Law and
    Justice): official PDFs of the Constitution, Acts and their amendments. No terms are published on the store itself
    (robots.txt 404, read 2026-11-21); the Department's site legislative.gov.in could not be read from here (HTTP 403,
    2026-11-02), so its website policy has not been read. Files are used only where a reachable page or the store's
    own listing links them.
  Internet Archive, archive.org: scans and metadata of official publications, used as a mirror and credited as such,
    with the official source recorded where the item names one. The gazetteofindia collection (uploaded by Public
    Resource, crawler github.com/sushant354/egazette) carries no licence statement on its items (read 2026-11-21); its
    content is official gazette matter (2.1 (i)) or a Government work before 1966 (2.2). Older Acts, codes and
    regulations come from scans of official editions in the Digital Library of India and other library collections on
    archive.org; these are Government works before 1966 (2.2). Lexifina makes its own text from the scan's text layer,
    or by its own OCR where there is none; archive.org's own OCR text is not used.
  Indian Supreme Court judgments and Indian High Court judgments (AWS Open Data: registry.opendata.aws/indian-supreme-
    court-judgments and registry.opendata.aws/indian-high-court-judgments; github.com/vanga/indian-supreme-court-
    judgments and github.com/vanga/indian-high-court-judgments; read 2026-11-21): licensed under Creative Commons
    Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Attribution: "Indian
    Supreme Court Judgments" and "Indian High Court Judgments", by their maintainers (Dattam Labs), from the AWS Open Data
    Registry, CC BY 4.0. The datasets were collected from scr.sci.gov.in and judgments.ecourts.gov.in; their PDFs are
    recompressed copies, not byte-identical official copies. Commits from them carry a Mirror: trailer. Lexifina's
    changes: text extracted from the PDFs, one file per judgment, protected case types dropped (2.3).
  Government Open Data Licence - India (GODL), notified in the Gazette of India, Extraordinary, 13 February 2017
    (Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology notification of 10 February 2017): data published under it
    may be used, adapted and shared free of charge, including commercially, with an attribution statement naming the
    provider, the source, the licence and the URL; it does not cover personal information, official symbols or data
    the provider may not license. It applies to datasets published under it (data.gov.in); where a source in this
    repository says it publishes under GODL, its attribution is given with that source.
  Supreme Court of India, www.sci.gov.in (website policies, read through a search result 2026-11-21): "The contents
    on this website shall not be reproduced partially or fully, without duly & prominently acknowledging the source."
    Judgments checked against or taken from the Court's own copies name it as the source in each commit.

