    Attribution: Source: Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India, irdai.gov.in.
  Law and Judiciary Department, Government of Maharashtra, https://old-lj.maharashtra.gov.in (used for states/maharashtra/)
    Terms (read 2026-11-22, https://old-lj.maharashtra.gov.in/1099/Terms-and-Condition): the Terms and Conditions
    page has no reproduction terms; its footer reads (in Marathi) that the site is the official website of the Law
    and Judiciary Department, all rights reserved. Acts are published with original matter (2.1 (ii)) and the
    Department's reprints are its official English texts.
  National Company Law Appellate Tribunal (NCLAT), https://nclat.nic.in/judgement-data (used for tribunals/nclat/)
    Terms (read 2026-11-22, https://nclat.nic.in/copyright-policy): copyright policy: material on the portal may be
    reproduced free of charge in any format without specific permission, if reproduced accurately and not in a
    derogatory or misleading way, with the source prominently acknowledged; third-party material excluded. Orders
    are taken under 2.1 (iv).
    Attribution: Source: National Company Law Appellate Tribunal, nclat.nic.in.
  Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA), https://www.pfrda.org.in (used for regulators/pfrda/)
    Terms (read 2026-11-21, https://www.pfrda.org.in/web/pfrda/terms-and-conditions): terms and conditions: content
    "should not be considered a legal statement or used for legal purposes"; "(c) Copyright PFRDA. All rights
    reserved." Regulations and notifications are Gazette matter (2.1 (i)); circulars are taken as official text with
    the source named in each commit.
  State and union-territory gazettes (Internet Archive copies), https://archive.org/search?query=identifier%3Ain.gazette.* (used for states/<state>/gazette/, union-territories/<ut>/gazette/)
    Terms (read 2026-11-21): the in.gazette.<state> collections on archive.org carry no licence statement; their
    content is official gazette matter (2.1 (i)). Each commit names the archive.org item as Source and the state's
    own gazette site as Official-Text; notices about private persons are not taken.
  Telecom Regulatory Authority of India (TRAI), https://www.trai.gov.in (used for regulators/trai/)
    Terms (read 2026-11-21, https://www.trai.gov.in/disclaimer): disclaimer: "it cannot be guaranteed that Material
