    TRAI. All rights reserved". Regulations and notifications are Gazette matter (2.1 (i)); directions are taken as
    official text with the source named in each commit.

3.1 Acts and the Constitution in this repository, as first published here

    The legal text is the Constitution of India, as published by the Legislative Department (Official Languages Wing),
    Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India:

      The Constitution of India [As on 1st May, 2024]
      Source: https://legislative.gov.in/constitution-of-india/
      File: https://cdnbbsr.s3waas.gov.in/s380537a945c7aaa788ccfcdf1b99b5d8f/uploads/2024/07/20240716890312078.pdf
      Retrieved 29 October 2026.

    The Constitution is the law of India and the text is published by the Government of India for public use.
    This repository makes no claim over it.

    Changes made by Lexifina: the PDF's text layer was read, split into one Markdown file per article, page headers
    and footnotes were removed, amendment footnote markers were stripped, and lines were rejoined into paragraphs.
    The wording is otherwise the Government's. Not an official copy.

    The Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 (Act 45 of 2023) is the law of India, as published in The Gazette of India,
    Extraordinary, Part II, Section 1, No. 53 (25 December 2023) by the Ministry of Law and Justice (Legislative Department):
      Source: https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2023/250883.pdf
      Retrieved 30 October 2026.
    The file carries no licence statement; the Act is published by the Government of India for general information.
    Changes made by Lexifina: the English text layer was read, split into one Markdown file per section, running headers,
    page numbers and the marginal notes were removed, and lines were rejoined into paragraphs. Not an official copy.

    The Companies Act, 2013 (Act 18 of 2013) is the law of India, as published in The Gazette of India, Extraordinary,
    Part II, Section 1 (30 August 2013) by the Ministry of Law and Justice (Legislative Department):
      Source: https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2013/E_27_2013_425.pdf
      Retrieved 30 October 2026.
    The file carries no licence statement; the Act is published by the Government of India for general information.
    Changes made by Lexifina: the English text layer was read, split into one Markdown file per section (Sections 1 to 470),
    running headers, page numbers and the marginal notes were removed, and lines were rejoined into paragraphs. The Schedules
    are not included. Not an official copy.

    The Industrial Relations Code, 2020 (Act 35 of 2020), the Code on Social Security, 2020 (Act 36 of 2020) and the
    Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020 (Act 37 of 2020) are the law of India, as published in
    The Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, Section 1 (29 September 2020) by the Ministry of Law and Justice
    (Legislative Department):
      Sources: https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2020/222118.pdf (Industrial Relations Code)
               https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2020/222111.pdf (Code on Social Security)
               https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2020/222112.pdf (Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code)
      Commencement notifications S.O. 5319(E), 5320(E) and 5321(E) of 21 November 2025 (Ministry of Labour and
      Employment): https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2025/267882.pdf, .../267883.pdf and .../267884.pdf
      Retrieved 2 November 2026.
    The files carry no licence statement. Changes made by Lexifina: the English text layer was read, split into one
    Markdown file per section, running headers, page numbers and the marginal notes were removed, and lines were rejoined
    into paragraphs. The Schedules are not included. Not an official copy.

    The further commencement of provisions of the Code on Wages, 2019 is recorded from notification S.O. 5322(E),
    Ministry of Labour and Employment, Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, Section 3(ii), 21 November 2025:
      Source: https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2025/267885.pdf
      Retrieved 2 November 2026.
    The notification changes when the provisions it lists operate, without changing their words.

    The Income-tax Act, 2025 (Act 30 of 2025) is the law of India, as published in The Gazette of India, Extraordinary,
    Part II, Section 1, No. 35 (21 August 2025) by the Ministry of Law and Justice (Legislative Department):
      Source: https://egazette.gov.in/WriteReadData/2025/265620.pdf
      Retrieved 2 November 2026.
    The file carries no licence statement. Changes made by Lexifina: the English text layer was read, split into one
    Markdown file per section, running headers, page numbers and the marginal notes were removed, lines were rejoined
    into paragraphs, and tables were flattened to one cell per line. The Schedules are not included. Not an official copy.

    Reuse under Indian copyright law. The Copyright Act, 1957, section 52(1)(q), provides that the following do not
    constitute an infringement of copyright:
      "(q) the reproduction or publication of—
       (i) any matter which has been published in any Official Gazette except an Act of a Legislature;
       (ii) any Act of a Legislature subject to the condition that such Act is reproduced or published together with any
            commentary thereon or any other original matter;"
    This repository publishes the Acts together with original matter: the per-version notes, the commit records of when
    each provision came into force and which law made it, the tables in data/, and the tools in tools/. The e-Gazette
    (egazette.gov.in) states that the Gazette of India "can be accessed free of cost by the general public being available
    in the public domain"; neither it nor the files state a prohibition on reproduction.
